      "name": "Ghoul Fever",
      "category": "offensive",
      "traits": [
        "disease"
      ],
      "text": "Saving Throw DC 29 Fortitude save\n\n---\n\nStage 1 carrier with no ill effect (1 day)\n\nStage 2 2d6 void damage and regains half as many Hit Points from all healing (1 day)\n\nStage 3 as stage 2 (1 day)\n\nStage 4 2d6 void damage and gains no benefit from healing (1 day)\n\nStage 5 as stage 4 (1 day)\n\nStage 6 dead, and rises as a Ghoul the next midnight."
    },
    {
      "kind": "ability",
      "name": "Profane Paralysis",
      "category": "offensive",
      "traits": [
        "incapacitation",
        "occult"
      ],
      "text": "Any living, non-elf creature hit by the profane ghoul's attack must attempt a DC 29 Fortitude save save.\n\n---\n\nCritical Success The creature is unaffected.\n\nSuccess The creature is Slowed 1.\n\nFailure The creature is Paralyzed. It can attempt a new save at the end of each of its turns, and the DC cumulatively decreases by 1 on each such save."
    },
    {
      "kind": "ability",
      "name": "Profane Whispers",
      "actions": 2,
      "category": "offensive",
      "traits": [
        "auditory",
        "mental",
        "occult"
      ],
      "text": "The ghoul whispers profane secrets of undeath. Living creatures within 10 feet of the ghoul take 2d8 persistent,mental damage. Those with ghoul fever must also succeed at a DC 29 Will save save or have the disease advance one step. The profane ghoul can't use Profane Whispers again for 24 hours."
